And for that, you need a new PR and big change to the whole llava_next implementation.

@zucchini-nlp @amyeroberts In some parallelism paradigm, if a batch of 2 samples, one has an image and the other one has no image. Then, if we split the batch into 2 minibatch and send to 2 gpus with `dist.broadcast`, the `pixel_values` of the no-image batch must be a tensor and cannot be None. In distributed broadcasting, can only broadcast gpu tensor and not None.

Still, you may revert this change and assume that any trainer will set pixel_values to None before sending to `model.forward`.

If you go this path, @zucchini-nlp can help revert it.

